ing a red card than light-skinned players (95% CI -0.02 to 0.34; p=0.083)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 9, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[15, 15]], "assertion": "the adjusted odds ratio is 1.142 (95% CI 0.983 to 1.327; p=0.083)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["odds ratio"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 10, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[16, 16]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is not supported because the confidence interval includes zero and p=0.083 exceeds the 0.05 threshold", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 11, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[17, 19]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 12, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[20, 21]], "note": "section 1 heading"}, {"id": 13, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[22, 23]], "assertion": "dark-skinned was defined as skin tone ≥0.50 and light-skinned as ≤0.25 for the risk-difference estimand, adjusting for covariates", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone threshold"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 14, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[24, 24]], "note": "Result label"}, {"id": 15, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[25, 25]], "assertion": "the risk difference is 0.1595 percentage points", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 16, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[26, 26]], "assertion": "the 95% CI for the risk difference is -0.0209 to 0.3399 percentage points", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["risk difference CI"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 17, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[27, 27]], "assertion": "the standard error of the risk difference is 0.000920 on the probability scale", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["standard error"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 18, 