"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 104, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[160, 160]], "assertion": "(truncated fragment) a variable including mean IAT was a strong predictor (p<0.001), taken to confirm that referee-country racial attitudes matter for red card decisions", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["meanIAT"], "confidence": "low", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 105, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[161, 163]], "note": "section divider (text truncated between sections 4-7)"}, {"id": 106, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[164, 165]], "note": "section 7 heading"}, {"id": 107, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[166, 167]], "note": "7.1 Measurement Issues heading"}, {"id": 108, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[168, 168]], "note": "Skin tone rating label"}, {"id": 109, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[169, 169]], "assertion": "skin tone was rated from profile photos rather than in-person observation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["skin tone rating source"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 110, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[170, 170]], "note": "caveat that photo ratings may not reflect referees' in-game perception"}, {"id": 111, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[171, 171]], "assertion": "raters were blind to the research question when rating skin tone", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["rater blinding"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 112, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[172, 173]], "assertion": "only 1,586 of 2,053 players (77%) had photos available", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["photo availability"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 113, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[174, 174]], "note": "Red card outcome label"}, {"id": 114, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[175, 175]], "assertion": "the red card outcome was aggregated across all games in a dyad (1 to 47 games)", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["red card aggregation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 115, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[176, 176]], "assertion": "the red card outcome measure did not capture the severity or context of the fouls that led to red cards", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["red card severity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 116, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[177, 178]], "note": "caveat that outcome may mix direct red cards and second yellows"}, {"id": 117, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[179, 179]], "note": "Exposure control label"}, {"id": 118, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "the analysis controlled for the number of games played", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["games"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [119]}, {"id": 119, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[180, 180]], "assertion": "the analysis did not control for playing time within games", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["playing time"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [118]}, {"id": 120, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[181, 181]], "note": "reasoning that more minutes gives more red-card opportunity"}, {"id": 121, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[182, 183]], "assertion": "the analysis had no data on player aggression, foul history, or playing style", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["aggression", "foul history", "playing style"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 122, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[184, 185]], "note": "7.2 Confounding heading"}, {"id": 123, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[186, 186]], "note": "Residual confounding label"}, {"id": 124, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[187, 187]], "assertion": "within-position variation in playing style was not captured because position categories are broad", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["position variation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 125, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[188, 188]], "assertion": "there was no measure of player reputation or prior disciplinary record with specific referees", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["player reputation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 126, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[189, 189]], "assertion": "team-level factors such as team playing style or coach instructions were not controlled", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["team-level factors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 127, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[190, 191]], "assertion": "match-level factors such as match importance or score differential were not controlled", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["match-level factors"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 128, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[192, 192]], "note": "Selection bias label"}, {"id": 129, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[193, 193]], "assertion": "dyads without skin tone ratings were excluded from the analysis", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusion: missing skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 130, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[194, 195]], "assertion": "the middle skin tone category (0.375, 5,609 dyads) was excluded from the analysis", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exclusion: intermediate skin tone"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 131, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[196, 196]], "note": "Ecological fallacy label"}, {"id": 132, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[197, 197]], "note": "IAT and explicit bias measures are country-level aggregates from online samples"}, {"id": 133, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[198, 200]], "note": "caveat that country-level bias measures may not reflect individual referees"}, {"id": 134, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[201, 202]], "note": "7.3 Statistical Issues heading"}, {"id": 135, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[203, 203]], "note": "Clustering label"}, {"id": 136, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[204, 204]], "assertion": "cluster-robust standard errors accounted for within-player correlation", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["cluster-robust SE"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [137]}, {"id": 137, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[204, 204]], "assertion": "the analysis did not account for within-referee correlation", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["within-referee correlation"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [136]}, {"id": 138, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[205, 205]], "assertion": "referee random effects were not modeled", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee random effects"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 139, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[206, 206]], "assertion": "several sensitivity analyses were conducted", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": [140]}, {"id": 140, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[206, 206]], "assertion": "no formal adjustment for multiple testing was applied across the sensitivity analyses", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["multiple testing adjustment"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [139]}, {"id": 141, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[207, 208]], "note": "Power label"}, {"id": 142, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[209, 209]], "assertion": "the outcome is rare: 1.25% of dyads have red cards", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["outcome rarity"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 143, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[210, 210]], "assertion": "the overall sample is large, but the dark-skin group is only 24% of the sample", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample composition"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 144, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[211, 212]], "note": "caveat about possible underpowering for subgroup analyses"}, {"id": 145, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[213, 213]], "note": "Functional form label"}, {"id": 146, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[214, 215]], "note": "caveat about logistic regression linearity assumption and possible non-linear effects"}, {"id": 147, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[216, 217]], "assertion": "a sensitivity analysis treating skin tone as a continuous variable was statistically significant", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone analysis"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 148, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[218, 219]], "note": "7.4 Generalizability heading"}, {"id": 149, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[220, 220]], "note": "Sample limitations label"}, {"id": 150, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[221, 222]], "note": "caveat about single-season, four-league scope limiting generalizability"}, {"id": 151, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[223, 223]], "assertion": "the analysis included no data on women's soccer (only male players)", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["women's soccer data"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 152, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[224, 225]], "note": "caveat that professional-only scope may not generalize to amateur/youth soccer"}, {"id": 153, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[226, 226]], "note": "Contextual factors label"}, {"id": 154, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "background", "lines": [[227, 227]], "note": "VAR was not yet implemented in 2012-2013"}, {"id": 155, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "hedging", "lines": [[228, 230]], "note": "caveat about policies/training changes and cultural context since data collection"}, {"id": 156, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[231, 232]], "note": "7.5 Potential Violations of Assumptions heading"}, {"id": 157, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[233, 233]], "note": "Logistic regression assumptions label"}, {"id": 158, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[234, 234]], "assertion": "the independence-assumption violation from clustering was addressed using robust standard errors", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["independence assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 159, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[235, 235]], "assertion": "linearity of continuous predictors on the log-odds scale was not extensively tested", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["linearity assumption"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 160, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[236, 236]], "assertion": "multicollinearity was checked and no issues were detected", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["multicollinearity check"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 161, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[237, 238]], "assertion": "the overall sample size is large but the outcome event is rare", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sample size adequacy"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 162, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[239, 239]], "note": "Missing data assumptions label"}, {"id": 163, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[240, 240]], "assertion": "median imputation for height/weight assumes the data are missing at random", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["MAR assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 164, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[241, 241]], "assertion": "zero-filling for IAT/explicit bias assumes the small amount of missingness is ignorable", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["ignorability assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 165, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[242, 243]], "assertion": "exclusion of dyads with missing skin tone assumes available photos are representative", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["representativeness assumption"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 166, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[244, 245]], "note": "7.6 Alternative Explanations heading"}, {"id": 167, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[246, 247]], "note": "transition sentence introducing alternative explanations"}, {"id": 168, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[248, 248]], "assertion": "foul severity was not measured, leaving possible confounding by foul severity unaddressed", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["foul severity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 169, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[249, 249]], "note": "speculative alternative explanation: position-related confounding within broad categories"}, {"id": 170, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[250, 250]], "note": "speculative alternative explanation: stereotype threat"}, {"id": 171, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[251, 251]], "assertion": "player/opponent ability was not controlled for", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["player ability"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 172, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[252, 252]], "assertion": "pre-existing referee-player conflicts or communication issues were not captured", "polarity": "did_not", "targets": ["referee-player interactions"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 173, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[253, 255]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 174, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[256, 257]], "note": "section 8 heading"}, {"id": 175, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[258, 259]], "note": "transition sentence introducing strengths"}, {"id": 176, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[260, 260]], "assertion": "the dataset is large and comprehensive: 119,012 dyads across 4 countries and 1,508 players", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["dataset size"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 177, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[261, 261]], "assertion": "red cards were treated as a clear, objective outcome requiring no coding judgment", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["outcome objectivity"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 178, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[262, 262]], "assertion": "skin tone ratings were high quality, from two independent raters with excellent reliability (r=0.92)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["rating quality"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 179, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[263, 263]], "assertion": "number of games was treated as a well-measured, critical confounder", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["exposure control"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 180, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[264, 264]], "assertion": "multiple relevant covariates were included: position, physical characteristics, league, and country-level bias", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["covariates"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 181, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[265, 265]], "assertion": "logistic regression with cluster-robust SEs and marginal effects was used as an appropriate statistical method", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["statistical methods"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 182, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[266, 266]], "assertion": "all exclusions, transformations, and decisions were documented transparently", "polarity": "did", "targets": ["reporting transparency"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 183, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[267, 267]], "assertion": "multiple operationalizations were tested in sensitivity analyses and results were generally robust", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["sensitivity analyses"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 184, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "framing", "lines": [[268, 269]], "note": "motivational statement about real-world importance of the topic"}, {"id": 185, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[270, 271]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 186, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[272, 273]], "note": "section 9 heading"}, {"id": 187, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "other", "lines": [[274, 283]], "note": "list of recommendations for future research, not describing the present analysis"}, {"id": 188, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[284, 285]], "note": "section divider"}, {"id": 189, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "heading", "lines": [[286, 287]], "note": "section 10 heading"}, {"id": 190, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[288, 289]], "assertion": "overall, the analysis of 119,012 dyads provides inconclusive evidence for the hypothesis: the point estimate suggests a small positive association (~0.16pp, 17% relative increase from a 0.94% baseline) but the 95% CI includes zero and p=0.083 exceeds 0.05", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["overall conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 191, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[290, 290]], "assertion": "the hypothesis is not supported at α=0.05; the null hypothesis of no difference cannot be rejected", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["conclusion"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [192]}, {"id": 192, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[290, 290]], "assertion": "a sensitivity analysis treating skin tone as continuous reached statistical significance (p=0.022)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["continuous skin tone analysis"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": [191]}, {"id": 193, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[291, 293]], "assertion": "country-level implicit bias is strongly associated with red card rates (p<0.001), interpreted as support for continued monitoring and possible bias-reduction training for referees", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["implicit bias association"], "confidence": "medium", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 194, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[294, 294]], "assertion": "the effect direction is positive, favoring the hypothesis", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect direction"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 195, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[295, 295]], "assertion": "the effect magnitude is small (0.16 percentage points absolute, 17% relative)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["effect magnitude"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 196, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[296, 296]], "assertion": "statistical uncertainty is moderate because the CI includes zero and p=0.08", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["statistical uncertainty"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 197, "kind": "claim", "lines": [[297, 297]], "assertion": "the final classification is NOT SUPPORTED (inconclusive)", "polarity": "found", "targets": ["final classification"], "confidence": "high", "shares_lines_with": []}, {"id": 198, "kind": "nonclaim", "subtype": "boilerplate", "lines": [[298, 299]], "note": "tool-output wrapper closing tag"}]}}